SQL SERVER PROCESS KILL WHEN SPID UTILIZING FOR MEMORY AND DISK SPACE


STEP 1
========
•	Execute the below query to identify which SPID has been blocking.
•	Then execute the KILL command with SPID. 
SELECT 
    session_id AS SPID,
    blocking_session_id AS BlockingSPID,
    wait_type,
    wait_time,
    status
KILL <SPID>;


STEP 2
=========
•	Execute the below query and after execution list of SPID and Commands running currently.
•	To find which CPU time and DISK IO is high and status is Sleeping.
•	EXEC sp_who2;
•	Then execute KILL command with SPID which is high CPUtime , DISKIO and status Sleeping
KILL <SPID>;
